    "result_text": "Build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is entirely **derived** from two fields the owner already carries (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), I modeled it the same way as the existing derived presentation fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than persisting it \u2014 this keeps it always consistent and seed-independent, matching the test's intent.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (right after `customerCode`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `@AfterMapping addMembershipNumber(...)` method that sets `customerCode + \"-M\" + yy`, where `yy` is `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` zero-padded to two digits. It leaves the value null if either source field is absent (defensive; in practice `saveOwner` always populates both).\n\nThe single acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
